<file path="docs/preview-mode-test-plan.md">
# Preview Mode (AUTH_MODE=mock) Test Plan

This document tracks every Clerk-dependent server entry point and how it
behaves when `AUTH_MODE=mock` (preview / reviewer mode). The goal is that
no path should throw because `CLERK_SECRET_KEY` (or any other Clerk
configuration) is missing.

## Audit results

Files that import from `$lib/server/clerk` or call `getClerkClient`:

| File | Behavior under AUTH_MODE=mock |
| --- | --- |
| `src/hooks.server.ts` | Short-circuits at the top of `handle`: builds a mock auth + mock member from cookie overrides and skips `authenticateClerkRequest`, `getClerkClient`, `ensureMemberIdentity`, and `syncAndEnforceSessionLimit`. |
| `src/routes/api/clerk/webhook/+server.ts` | Returns HTTP 501 with a "disabled in preview mode" message before touching `verifyClerkWebhook`. |
| `src/routes/api/settings/sessions/[sessionId]/revoke/+server.ts` | Returns HTTP 501 with a preview-mode message before constructing a Clerk client. |
| `src/lib/server/session-security.ts` | Internal helper. Only invoked from the Clerk branch of `hooks.server.ts`; never reached in mock mode. |
| `src/lib/server/db/shivworks.ts` (`ensureMemberIdentity`) | Internal helper that needs a `ClerkClient`. Only invoked from the Clerk branch of `hooks.server.ts`; never reached in mock mode. The other consumers of this module (admin actions, webhook event handler) call sibling helpers like `claimImportedMemberProvision`, `upsertMemberFromWebhook`, and `getMemberByEmail` that do not require Clerk. |

The remaining server endpoints under `src/routes/api/**` and
`src/routes/**/+page.server.ts` (events RSVP, library progress, stripe
checkout/webhook, vip-call request, preview-identity, admin, dashboard,
library, live, settings, etc.) do not import from `$lib/server/clerk`
and rely on `event.locals.user` populated by the hook, which works in
both modes.

## Manual test checklist (AUTH_MODE=mock)

Run with `AUTH_MODE=mock` and no Clerk secrets configured. Each item
below was confirmed not to throw a 500 because of missing Clerk
credentials.

- Visit `/` and `/dashboard` while logged in as the mock member.
- Visit `/admin` (set `MOCK_ADMIN=1` or use the preview-identity cookie
  to switch to the admin role) and confirm the page renders.
- Submit `POST /api/preview-identity` to switch role/tier; reload pages
  to confirm overrides apply.
- Submit `POST /api/settings/sessions/<anything>/revoke` and confirm the
  endpoint returns `501 { error: "...preview mode..." }` instead of
  hitting Clerk.
- Submit `POST /api/clerk/webhook` (any payload) and confirm the
  endpoint returns `501 { error: "...preview mode..." }` instead of
  attempting `verifyWebhook`.
- Trigger an admin "Import members" action with a small CSV; verify
  that imported rows are claimed/queued without contacting Clerk
  (claim path uses `claimImportedMemberProvision`, which only touches
  the database).
- Visit `/settings/sessions` and confirm the active-session list loads
  for the mock user (the page reads from D1 only).

## Production safeguard

`resolveAuthMode` already throws when `AUTH_MODE=mock` is set with
`NODE_ENV=production`, so the preview short-circuits above can never
silently disable Clerk in a live deployment.
</file>

<file path="migrations/0014_recognition_day_bucket.sql">
-- Switch recognitions uniqueness from (giver_id, message_id) to
-- (giver_id, message_id, day_bucket) so a member may recognize the same
-- post once per UTC day rather than once forever.

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS recognitions_new (
  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
  giver_id TEXT NOT NULL,
  recipient_id TEXT NOT NULL,
  message_id TEXT NOT NULL,
  day_bucket TEXT NOT NULL,
  created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,
  UNIQUE(giver_id, message_id, day_bucket),
  FOREIGN KEY(giver_id) REFERENCES members(clerk_user_id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  FOREIGN KEY(recipient_id) REFERENCES members(clerk_user_id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  FOREIGN KEY(message_id) REFERENCES messages(id) ON DELETE CASCADE
);

INSERT INTO recognitions_new (id, giver_id, recipient_id, message_id, day_bucket, created_at)
SELECT
  id,
  giver_id,
  recipient_id,
  message_id,
